NNAAMMEE
     ppoorrttggeenn — port modules on the fly

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ppoorrttggeenn [--mm _m_a_k_e_o_p_t] _t_y_p_e _m_o_d_u_l_e_-_n_a_m_e

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppoorrttggeenn utility creates ports for the given _m_o_d_u_l_e_-_n_a_m_e from _t_y_p_e
     module framework.  The module is downloaded, analyzed and translated into
     a port.  Any missing dependencies are handled recursively.  New ports
     will land under ${PORTSDIR}/mystuff.  The PORTSDIR value will be taken
     from current user environment, and defaults to _/_u_s_r_/_p_o_r_t_s.

     The options are as follows:

     --mm _m_a_k_e_o_p_t
             Pass _m_a_k_e_o_p_t to make(1) invocations while resolving missing de‐
             pendencies, mostly useful with ‘FETCH_PACKAGES=’ to avoid build‐
             ing everything from scratch.

     The ppoorrttggeenn utility currently supports the following _t_y_p_e values:

           pp55 for Perl modules on CPAN.
           rruubbyy for Ruby gems.
           ggoo for Go modules.

     A ggoo module may be used with an _@_v_e_r_s_i_o_n suffix to specify a tag or
     branch to port.  The default suffix is _@_l_a_t_e_s_t, which is interpreted as
     the latest release.

     The following packages must be installed prior to the invocation of
     ppoorrttggeenn:

           ssqqllppoorrttss
           pp55--DDBBII
           pp55--DDBBDD--SSQQLLiittee

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The ppoorrttggeenn utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     The following command will download the latest version of Config::Auto‐
     Conf from CPAN, parse it and create a port for it:

           ppoorrttggeenn p5 Config::AutoConf

